      "role": "user",
      "content": "im so freaking worried my son is so sick and im just sitting here crying. his ear is so swollen and he's been so lethargic and won't even play like normal. the doctor said 40mg per kg a day for his 15kg weight so i calculated 600mg total... but the amoxicillin bottle says 125mg per 5ml. \n\nwhen i do the math it says he needs 24ml?? 24ml seems like such a huge amount of liquid for a little guy, i'm scared it'll make him sick or he'll just throw it all up. is there any way to do a smaller amount so he doesn't have to swallow so much? and is it normal that he's so sleepy/lethargic? i'm just so lost and dont want to mess up his meds. pls help",
